{"name":"Napa Wine","hex":"#5d4149","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"napa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brassica rapa subsp. pekinensis, a kind of Chinese cabbage."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["napa leather"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/napa"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Napa Valley AVA","blocks":[{"text":"Napa Valley is an American Viticultural Area (AVA) in Napa County, California. It was established as the nation's second, the state and county's initial appellation on January 28, 1981 by the U.S. Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms (ATF), Treasury after reviewing the 1978 petition submitted by the Napa Valley Vintners and the Napa Valley Grape Growers Association proposing the viticultural area named \"Napa Valley.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/TTB_Map_Napa_Valley_AVA.png/330px-TTB_Map_Napa_Valley_AVA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napa_Valley_AVA","wikidata":"Q1151105"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg/500px-Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg/1280px-Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg/500px-Napa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grapes in a Napa Valley vineyard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANapa_Valley_grapes_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg/500px-Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg/1280px-Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg/500px-Napa_Valley_Opus_One_Photo_Don_Ramey_Logan_01.jpg?utm